==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-beezer.ogg|Audio (AU)}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːzə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
{{unk|en}}, perhaps from {{der|en|es|cabeza||head}}, though the meaning “head” appears to somewhat postdate “nose” in English.<ref>{{cite-book|last=Ayto|first=John|year=1998|title=Oxford Dictionary of Slang|entry=beezer|isbn=019280104X|pages=1, 3}}</ref> {{etydate|1908|nodot=1}}, originally apparently as American [[boxing]] slang. Various sources have suggested a borrowing, perhaps by American sailors or marines, from {{ncog|cmn|鼻子|sc=Hani|t=nose|tr=bízi}} ([[:File:zh-bízi.ogg|audio]]).<ref>{{cite-book|year=2008|last=Hendrickson|first=Robert|entry=beezer|title=The Facts on File Encyclopedia of Word and Phrase Origins|edition=4th|isbn=9780816069668|page=73}}</ref><ref>{{cite-journal|year=1933|month=September|last=Anderson|first=Luther|title=Words With a Wanderlust|journal=Education|volume=54|page=39}}</ref> While the Mandarin may have reinforced an existing term,<ref>Compare for example {{cite-book|en|year=1993|last=Bollich|first=James|title=Bataan Death March: A Soldier’s Story|isbn=1589801679|page=132|pageurl=https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=WRgdCVYMbjIC&pg=PA132}}</ref> an ultimate derivation from Mandarin is improbable given the context and time frame of early use.

