# [[nose|Nose]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1913|title=Kid Ivanhoe|journal={{w|Adventure (magazine)|Adventure}}|volume=7|page=131|text=“In der '''beezer''', Casey, slam him in der '''beezer'''!” ¶ At the ropes Casey fought back, but was obliged to clinch.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1919|author=Charles Emmett Van Loan|title=Taking the Count: Prize Ring Stories|page=183|text=“Now, don’t be turnin’ up that busted '''beezer''' of yours so proud an’ haughty.{{nb...}}”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1937|author=Damon Runyon|title=A Piece of Pie
|passage=I am paying no attention to them, because they are drinking local ale, and talking loud, and long ago I learn that when a Boston character is engaged in aleing himself up, it is a good idea to let him alone, because the best you can get out of him is maybe a boff on the '''beezer'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1960|author=w:P. G. Wodehouse|title=w:Jeeves in the Offing|chapter=V
|passage=She had an ink spot on her nose, the result of working on her novel of suspense. It is virtually impossible to write a novel of suspense without getting a certain amount of ink on the '''beezer'''. Ask Agatha Christie or anyone.}}
# [[head|Head]].
#* {{quote-book|en|date=24 July 1921|author=Eleanor Pray|chapter=[Letter home]|editor=Birgitta Ingemanson|title=Letters from Vladivostok, 1894–1930|year_published=2013|page=98|pageurl=https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=nsYVCgAAQBAJ&pg=PA98|text=We were beating up into the wind, when Captain Pray decided to tack, and her concise order to me was “Duck your '''beezer'''!” and while I was wondering which part of the boat a '''beezer''' was, the boom just missed the top of my head and she remarked, “I ''told'' you to duck.”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1928|author=Robert Joyce Tasker|title=Grimhaven|page=110|text=“{{...}} If the hogs ate your '''beezer''' with all the phony ideas you’ve got in it, they’d croak!”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1937|brackets=on|entry=Slang: American Slang|title=w:The Encyclopædia Britannica|edition=14th|volume=20|page=768|text='''Beezer''', head}}

